    "body": "## Overview\n\n`max_tool_calls` is declared on `ResponsesRequest` and echoed back in\nresponse objects, but it had no consumer anywhere in serving code: the\nbuiltin tool loop in `_generate_with_builtin_tools` is an unbounded\n`while True` whose only exit condition is the model itself stopping to\ncall tools. This PR enforces the declared bound and adds `ge=0`\nvalidation on the field.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The builtin tool loop now stops after exactly `max_tool_calls` builtin\n  tool calls have been executed.\n- `max_tool_calls` rejects negative values with 422 at the protocol layer\n  (`Field(default=None, ge=0)`).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Before the fix: a request carrying `max_tool_calls=2` against a model\n  that emits a builtin tool call on every turn performed an unbounded\n  number of engine round-trips (observed 50+ under an external emergency\n  cap; the loop itself has no limit), while the request carried and\n  echoed `max_tool_calls=2` as if a quota were in effect.\n- After the fix: the loop exits after exactly `max_tool_calls` tool\n  calls (`sub_request + 1 >= max_tool_calls` check after\n  `context.append_tool_output`). Logic-level reproduction script and\n  loop-level unit test included in test runs.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: the field is declared (protocol.py `ResponsesRequest`),\nechoed in `ResponsesResponse`, and copied through sub-requests, but the\nserving loop never reads it. Each turn additionally re-derives\n`sampling_params.max_tokens` from the full remaining budget\n(`get_max_tokens(...)` at the bottom of the loop body), so nothing\nbounds the number of turns.\n\nThe check lives after `context.append_tool_output(tool_output)` so the\ntool result of the final allowed call is still appended to the context\nbefore exiting.\n\nThis PR was created with AI assistance; the submitter has reviewed and\ntakes responsibility for every line.\n",
